{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are fixing three photo bugs in this KISS app (TanStack Start + Nitro server, Neon Postgres). Work on the current branch cursor/photo-fixes. No DB migrations. No new paid services. Keep changes focused. Commit when done, push, open a PR to main.\n\n1) People's photos don't show in the orbit/home. Photos exist in phone_book.photo on the server but are never sent. In server.ts, phoneHome (around lines 1340-1411) returns inbox/sent without photo: add a phone_book.photo subselect for the counterpart (same pattern as the inbox query around lines 1292-1312), add `photo` to the KissRow/SentKiss types, and in src/routes/index.tsx mergeOrbit/photoOf (around 1141-1151) use the server photo, falling back to local. Also fix the backfill at index.tsx ~361-394: searchDirectory({q:\"\"}) returns photo:null because server.ts ~1201-1203 sets wantPhoto only when q>=2 chars or a phone lookup; allow photos when myPhone is set, and backfill for people known from the server, not only prev.orbit.\n\n2) Invite link preview (WhatsApp) shows the generic KISS image instead of the sender's card. Route src/routes/k.$from.tsx (~28-47) sets og:image=/c/<code> (relative). server/middleware/grok-pwa.ts via scripts/grok-pwa-shared.mjs (~line 435 stripShareMetaTags, lines 13-29 list, grokOgHeadTags 336-376 injected 445-448) strips all og/twitter tags and injects site defaults on every HTML page. Fix: skip the strip+inject when the page already sets its own og:image (or for /k/* paths), preferably in the Nitro middleware so a platform sync of the shared script doesn't undo it. Make og:image, og:image:secure_url and twitter:image absolute (origin + /c/<code>), add og:url, og:image:width 1200/height 630, twitter:card summary_large_image. Verify with curl -A \"WhatsApp/2.23.20.0\" against a local/preview /k/<code> that the head contains the per-link absolute og:image and not /og.jpg.\nSide fix: resolveShareLink only checks share_links; QR links /k/<code> come from qr_codes. Make it also resolve qr_codes codes.\n\n3) Photos are small/blurry. cropPhoto (src/lib/me.ts ~140-160) makes 280px q0.7; what's saved to Neon is shrinkDataUrl(data,160) (index.tsx ~810, ~830; contacts.ts ~68-93) at q0.62; index.tsx ~253 overwrites the local copy with the 160px server one on boot. Change: crop/save at 512px JPEG q0.8 (target under ~60KB), stop downgrading the local photo on boot when local is larger, raise limits safely: registerPhone slice(0,120000) in server.ts ~1123 must not silently truncate (raise to ~200000 and reject over-limit instead of cutting); saveMe drops orbit photos over 12000 chars (me.ts ~77) — raise sensibly. Fix CSS: styles.css ~355-362 sets own orbit photo to 6.25rem on phones, overriding kiss-ui.css 7.2rem; make the own photo at least 7.5rem on phones, and bump other people's orbit chips (kiss-orbit.tsx ~94, 3.25rem x0.85) to about 4rem. Share card (send-sheet.tsx ~158-177, buildKissCard) JPEG quality 0.55 -> 0.8.\n\nRun the build/typecheck before committing. In the PR body list each change and how to test it with 555 test numbers.\n\nPR title must be exactly: \"Photos: people photos in orbit, invite link preview with sender photo, sharper photos\". PR body: short English list of changes + test notes. Do NOT merge. Do NOT deploy. Do NOT write to any database. Do not commit docs/AGENT-PROMPT-PHOTOS.txt or any log files."}]},"session_id":"048e4607-7507-4c09-84b1-b33f77e5e581"}
