{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"toolu_01RcYEPFn7o3MTWCUcJLZKiz","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/naoryanko/kiss/kiss && cat > /tmp/pr-body.md <<'EOF'\n## Changes\n\n1. **People's photos in the orbit**\n   - `phoneHome` now returns the counterpart's `phone_book.photo` on inbox and sent rows (same subselect as `phoneInbox`), once per person to keep the payload small. `KissRow` and `SentKiss` have a new optional `photo` field.\n   - `mergeOrbit` uses the server photo first. Local and recent-contact photos are only a fallback.\n   - `searchDirectory` returns photos when `myPhone` is set. The home screen keeps those directory photos and fills in any orbit person without a face, including people who came from the server.\n\n2. **Invite link preview (WhatsApp) shows the sender's card**\n   - New `server/lib/share-aware-head.mjs` wraps the platform head injector. Pages that already set their own `og:image` keep their share tags, and only the PWA tags are added. Every other page still gets the site defaults. The Nitro middleware uses it, and so does the Vite dev plugin. It lives outside `scripts/` so a platform sync of `grok-pwa-shared.mjs` won't undo it.\n   - `/k/<code>` now uses absolute `og:image`, `og:image:secure_url` and `twitter:image` (origin + `/c/<code>`), and adds `og:url`. `og:image:width` 1200, `og:image:height` 630 and `twitter:card summary_large_image` are unchanged. The origin comes from `VITE_PUBLIC_HOSTNAME` when set, otherwise from the request's forwarded host.\n   - `resolveShareLink` and `getShareCard` also look up `qr_codes`, so personal QR links show the owner's name and photo.\n\n3. **Sharper photos**\n   - Photo crop and upload are now 512px JPEG at quality 0.8, stepping quality down only when needed to stay under about 60KB (`src/lib/jpeg.ts`). The 160px / 0.62 re-encode before saving to Neon is gone.\n   - On boot, a larger local photo is no longer replaced by a smaller server copy (older builds saved a 160px copy to Neon).\n   - `registerPhone` rejects photos over 200000 chars instead of cutting them off (a truncated data URL is a broken image).\n   - `saveMe` keeps orbit photos up to about 90000 chars (was 12000).\n   - CSS: your own orbit photo is 7.5rem on phones (was 6.25rem). Other people's chips show at about 4rem (4.7rem × the 0.85 scale).\n   - Share card (`buildKissCard`) JPEG quality goes from 0.55 to 0.8. Quality steps down only if the card would exceed the 350000-char limit in `createShareLink`.\n\nNo DB migrations, no new services.\n\n## How to test (555 numbers)\n\n- **Orbit photos:** On device A, sign in as `+1 555 555 0101`, add a photo, and send a kiss to `+1 555 555 0102`. On device B, sign in as `0102`, add a photo, and kiss back. Clear site data on A and reopen: B's face should appear in A's orbit right away (from the server, not localStorage), and the reverse on B.\n- **Invite preview:** From `0101` (with a photo), open Send, then copy the invite link `/k/<code>`. Run `curl -s -A \"WhatsApp/2.23.20.0\" https://<preview-host>/k/<code> | grep -aoE '<meta [^>]*(og|twitter):[^>]*>'`. `og:image` should be `https://<host>/c/<code>` and `/og.jpg` should not appear. `curl -I https://<host>/c/<code>` should return an image. Paste the link into WhatsApp to check the card shows the sender's photo.\n- **QR links:** Open `0101`'s QR code link `/k/<qr-code>`. The page should say it's from 0101's name, and `og:image` should be `/c/<qr-code>` with 0101's photo.\n- **Home page OG unchanged:** `curl -s -H 'accept: text/html' https://<host>/ | grep og:` still shows the site defaults.\n- **Sharpness:** Upload a large photo as `0101`. The saved photo (DevTools, localStorage `kiss-me-v2`) should be a 512×512 JPEG under about 80000 chars. Reload and it stays sharp. The own orbit photo is visibly bigger on a phone, and people chips are about 4rem.\n\nVerified locally (dev server with in-memory PGLite, no real database): `npm run typecheck` passes, `vite build` passes, and the script tests are unchanged from `main` (140 pass, 9 pre-existing failures). A WhatsApp-UA curl of `/k/<code>` returned `og:image=http://localhost:8091/c/<code>` with no `/og.jpg`, a QR code resolved to its owner, and `/` still got the platform defaults.\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head cursor/photo-fixes --title \"Photos: people photos in orbit, invite link preview with sender photo, sharper photos\" --body-file /tmp/pr-body.md","workingDirectory":"","timeout":60000,"toolCallId":"toolu_01RcYEPFn7o3MTWCUcJLZKiz","simpleCommands":["cd","cat","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/naoryanko/kiss/kiss"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/naoryanko/kiss/kiss"},{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"pr"},{"type":"word","value":"create"},{"type":"word","value":"--base"},{"type":"word","value":"main"},{"type":"word","value":"--head"},{"type":"word","value":"cursor/photo-fixes"},{"type":"word","value":"--title"},{"type":"string","value":"\"Photos: people photos in orbit, invite link preview with sender photo, sharper photos\""},{"type":"word","value":"--body-file"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/pr-body.md"}],"fullText":"gh pr create --base main --head cursor/photo-fixes --title \"Photos: people photos in orbit, invite link preview with sender photo, sharper photos\" --body-file /tmp/pr-body.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/pr-body.md"},{"operator":"","destinationFds":[],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"048e4607-7507-4c09-84b1-b33f77e5e581","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"efcc917a-a88a-45b2-852e-f591dfa7e0c7"}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"toolu_01RcYEPFn7o3MTWCUcJLZKiz","startedAtMs":"1790663166143"},"model_call_id":"efcc917a-a88a-45b2-852e-f591dfa7e0c7-67-ayio","session_id":"048e4607-7507-4c09-84b1-b33f77e5e581","timestamp_ms":1790663171779}
