{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three photo bugs are fixed and pushed to `cursor/photo-fixes`, and [PR #14](https://github.com/rept0rix/kiss/pull/14) is open against `main` with the exact title you gave. I didn't merge or deploy it, and I didn't commit `docs/AGENT-PROMPT-PHOTOS.txt`, `android/` or `ios/`.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- Typecheck and the Vite build pass.\n- The script tests give the same result as before my changes: 140 pass, 9 fail. The 9 failures were already there.\n- With a WhatsApp user agent, `curl` of `/k/<code>` returns `og:image=http://localhost:8091/c/<code>` plus `og:url`, with no `/og.jpg`. `/c/<code>` serves the image.\n- A QR code link now resolves to its owner's name and photo.\n- The home page still gets the site's default preview tags.\n\n**How I tested without touching a database:**\n- I ran the Vite build step on its own, because `npm run build` also runs `db:migrate`.\n- I ran the dev server on port 8091 with `DATABASE_URL` empty, so it used the throwaway in-memory database. Port 8080 was your other dev server from `/Users/naoryanko/kiss`, and I left it running.\n- I created one test share link and one QR code in that in-memory database. Both are gone now that the server is stopped.\n\n**Changes worth knowing about:**\n1. **Orbit photos:** `phoneHome` now sends each person's photo, but only once per person rather than on every kiss row. At about 60KB per photo, 60 rows would otherwise be several MB. `mergeOrbit` uses the server photo first. The directory backfill keeps its results in state, so people who come from the server get faces even if the orbit was empty when the backfill ran.\n2. **Invite preview:** the fix is a new file, `server/lib/share-aware-head.mjs`. It wraps the platform's tag injector and leaves a page alone if the page already sets its own `og:image`. It lives outside `scripts/`, so syncing the platform's shared script won't undo it. Both the production server middleware and the dev plugin use it. The absolute URL comes from `VITE_PUBLIC_HOSTNAME` when set, otherwise from the forwarded host. I didn't run the production build end to end, only the dev path.\n3. **Sharper photos:**\n   - Photos are now 512px JPEG at quality 0.8. A new helper in `src/lib/jpeg.ts` lowers quality only when needed to stay under about 60KB.\n   - The share card uses the same helper so it stays under the 350,000-character limit in `createShareLink`, which otherwise cuts the image off and breaks it.\n   - On the server, a photo that's too big is now rejected with an error instead of being cut off.\n   - People chips in the orbit are 4.7rem in CSS, because the orbit component draws them at 0.85 scale. That makes them about 4rem on screen.\n\nThe PR description lists each change with test steps using the 555 numbers.Both of those \"errors\" were expected, so nothing needs doing and [PR #14](https://github.com/rept0rix/kiss/pull/14) is unaffected.\n\n- **First dev server:** it exited right away because port 8080 was already in use by your other dev server in `/Users/naoryanko/kiss`. That's why I moved to port 8091.\n- **Port 8091 server:** I stopped it on purpose once the `curl` checks passed. It was using the throwaway in-memory database, so the test share link and QR code it held are gone."}]},"session_id":"048e4607-7507-4c09-84b1-b33f77e5e581"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":599639,"duration_api_ms":599639,"is_error":false,"result":"I'll start by reading the relevant server and client code for the three bugs.Now the client side: `index.tsx` around the boot hydration, backfill, save paths, and `mergeOrbit`.I have the full picture. Starting with the server: `phoneHome` photos, `searchDirectory` photos, `registerPhone` limit, QR resolution, and an origin helper for the invite page.Now `searchDirectory` photos, the `registerPhone` limit, and QR-code resolution.Now the invite route head tags with absolute URLs.Now the head injector wrapper that leaves pages with their own `og:image` alone, shared by the Nitro middleware and the dev Vite plugin.Now the client: `mergeOrbit` prefers the server photo.Now sharper photos. Checking import relationships before adding a shared JPEG encoder.Now the share card quality and CSS sizes.Typecheck passes. Running the build, lint, and the head-injector script tests.`npm run build` also runs `db:migrate`, so I'll run only the Vite build step with `DATABASE_URL` unset to avoid touching any database.Lint has only pre-existing warnings. Comparing the script test results against the unmodified branch to confirm that failure is pre-existing.Script tests are unchanged (140 pass, 9 pre-existing failures, same as before my edits). Now the Vite build with `node_modules/.bin` on the PATH.Build succeeds. To verify the invite preview with curl I'll run the dev server locally; first I'm checking that it can't pick up a real `DATABASE_URL` from an env file.`.env` has no database URL, so the local server uses throwaway in-memory PGLite. Starting it.Server is up. First check: an unknown code (no DB write needed) should now keep the page's own absolute share tags.The platform defaults are no longer injected, but the URLs are still relative and `og:url` is missing, so I'm checking the dev log.Port 8080 was already taken by another process, so those results came from something else. Checking what it is.That's your separate dev server from `/Users/naoryanko/kiss`; I'll leave it alone and run this checkout on port 8091.Unknown codes now emit absolute URLs and `og:url`. For a real per-link check I'll create one share link in the throwaway in-memory PGLite through the app's own server function.Created share link `zsbgy` in the in-memory database. Now the WhatsApp crawler check against it, plus the card image itself.The invite page is correct: absolute per-link `og:image`, no `/og.jpg`, and `/c/zsbgy` serves the card. Confirming the home page still gets the platform tags.QR links now resolve to the owner (\"QR Tester\") with a per-code image. Stopping the local server and committing.All three photo bugs are fixed and pushed to `cursor/photo-fixes`, and [PR #14](https://github.com/rept0rix/kiss/pull/14) is open against `main` with the exact title you gave. I didn't merge or deploy it, and I didn't commit `docs/AGENT-PROMPT-PHOTOS.txt`, `android/` or `ios/`.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- Typecheck and the Vite build pass.\n- The script tests give the same result as before my changes: 140 pass, 9 fail. The 9 failures were already there.\n- With a WhatsApp user agent, `curl` of `/k/<code>` returns `og:image=http://localhost:8091/c/<code>` plus `og:url`, with no `/og.jpg`. `/c/<code>` serves the image.\n- A QR code link now resolves to its owner's name and photo.\n- The home page still gets the site's default preview tags.\n\n**How I tested without touching a database:**\n- I ran the Vite build step on its own, because `npm run build` also runs `db:migrate`.\n- I ran the dev server on port 8091 with `DATABASE_URL` empty, so it used the throwaway in-memory database. Port 8080 was your other dev server from `/Users/naoryanko/kiss`, and I left it running.\n- I created one test share link and one QR code in that in-memory database. Both are gone now that the server is stopped.\n\n**Changes worth knowing about:**\n1. **Orbit photos:** `phoneHome` now sends each person's photo, but only once per person rather than on every kiss row. At about 60KB per photo, 60 rows would otherwise be several MB. `mergeOrbit` uses the server photo first. The directory backfill keeps its results in state, so people who come from the server get faces even if the orbit was empty when the backfill ran.\n2. **Invite preview:** the fix is a new file, `server/lib/share-aware-head.mjs`. It wraps the platform's tag injector and leaves a page alone if the page already sets its own `og:image`. It lives outside `scripts/`, so syncing the platform's shared script won't undo it. Both the production server middleware and the dev plugin use it. The absolute URL comes from `VITE_PUBLIC_HOSTNAME` when set, otherwise from the forwarded host. I didn't run the production build end to end, only the dev path.\n3. **Sharper photos:**\n   - Photos are now 512px JPEG at quality 0.8. A new helper in `src/lib/jpeg.ts` lowers quality only when needed to stay under about 60KB.\n   - The share card uses the same helper so it stays under the 350,000-character limit in `createShareLink`, which otherwise cuts the image off and breaks it.\n   - On the server, a photo that's too big is now rejected with an error instead of being cut off.\n   - People chips in the orbit are 4.7rem in CSS, because the orbit component draws them at 0.85 scale. That makes them about 4rem on screen.\n\nThe PR description lists each change with test steps using the 555 numbers.Both of those \"errors\" were expected, so nothing needs doing and [PR #14](https://github.com/rept0rix/kiss/pull/14) is unaffected.\n\n- **First dev server:** it exited right away because port 8080 was already in use by your other dev server in `/Users/naoryanko/kiss`. That's why I moved to port 8091.\n- **Port 8091 server:** I stopped it on purpose once the `curl` checks passed. It was using the throwaway in-memory database, so the test share link and QR code it held are gone.","session_id":"048e4607-7507-4c09-84b1-b33f7